**Problem Statement

Some Jobcentre customers may be interested in gaining employment but lack the confidence, recent work experience, application skills or understanding of the opportunities available to them.

**Potential participants may also be unsure about:

*What the Movement to Work programme involves
*What they will be expected to do
*How the programme will benefit them
*What skills they will develop
*Which local employers or sectors may be available
*How they could travel to local employment opportunities
*Whether they are ready to return to a workplace environment

Existing information may not explain the programme in a clear, engaging and easy-to-understand way. This can make it harder for Jobcentre staff to promote the programme and harder for customers to recognise how taking 
part could support their career development.

The project will address this problem by creating an accessible and engaging website that clearly communicates the structure, activities and benefits of the Movement to Work programme.
The website should help potential participants understand that the programme is a supportive first step towards gaining experience, learning new skills, building confidence and improving their CV.
